  "body": "Found in the research of #3351. Refs #3351. This is a follow-up, not a sub-issue of the plan.\n\n## What is open\n\nThe plan of #3351 admits a tapered ball nose only in the 3-axis 3D Finish (#3374). These kinds stay refused by name for a tip-formed `Taper` and a `FormMill`:\n\n- Swarf and Advanced Swarf: a tapered flat end mill is a usual tool for drafted walls. The flank line of the cone, not a cylinder, must lie on the ruled wall.\n- 5-Axis Contour, 5-Axis Parallel, 5-Axis Flow, Multi-Axis Contour, the rotary kinds and Multi-Axis Rough: the tapered ball nose gives more reach and stiffness in deep cavities.\n- 3D Pocket: the rough ladder removes each level with a cylinder of the diameter; a tapered flank leaves ridges that the next level cuts with the flank.\n\n## Questions for the design\n\n- The swarf pose law with a cone flank (the contact line moves along the axis with the radius).\n- The tilt and avoidance laws (`crates/motion/src/multiaxis/avoid.rs`) with a cone body instead of a cylinder.\n- A rough ladder law for a tapered tool (a step-down that reads the flank).\n\nDepends on #3370\nDepends on #3371\nDepends on #3374\n\n## Done means\n\n- A design comment answers the three questions, and each admitted kind has its own sub-issue with a pinned test. Until then each kind refuses the new tools by name.\n",
